The process-local language component and its Zygisk integration are distributed
under GPL-3.0-only. The independently written duck-misc management crate and WebUI
retain the repository's MIT license. Management exchanges private JSON configuration
with the component and does not link the native engine.

The native component statically links LSPlant and DexBuilder under LGPL-3.0,
and parallel-hashmap under Apache-2.0. Their original notices remain applicable.
Source revisions and dependency retrieval are pinned in scripts/build-play-integrity.py.
The packaged Play Integrity SOURCE.txt links to that script at the exact build commit.

The ART prefix resolver adapts xDL's symbol lookup under its MIT license:
Copyright (c) 2020-2025 HexHacking Team. The existing pinned ShadowHook/xDL source
and license notices accompany the combined library. The build applies the prefix
lookup addition from native/xdl-prefix.inc; ELF parsing stays in xDL.

The combined library also includes the GPL-3.0-only Play Integrity component and
GPL-3.0-or-later Device Faker component. Their existing copyrights and license
notices are retained. Dependencies keep their own license terms.
